@startuml sequence_command_property
title Property access and command execution (ServiceProxy -> Service)

skinparam shadowing false

actor "User code" as User
participant "ServiceProxy\n(Python)" as PyProxy
participant "ServiceProxy\n(C++)" as Proxy
participant "Client\n(ZMQ REQ)" as Client
participant "Server\n(ZMQ REP)" as Server
participant "Service\n(C++)" as Svc
participant "User service code\n(Python getter/setter/command)" as PySvc

== Get property ==
User -> PyProxy : camera.exposure_time
PyProxy -> PyProxy : __getattr__ finds name\nin property_names
PyProxy -> Proxy : GetProperty("exposure_time")
Proxy -> Client : MakeRequest("get_property", request)
Client -> Server : ZMQ request [type, data]
Server -> Svc : dispatch to registered handler
Svc -> Svc : lookup m_Properties["exposure_time"]
Svc -> PySvc : invoke PropertyGetter
PySvc --> Svc : value
Svc --> Server : serialized Value (protobuf)
Server --> Client : ZMQ reply
Client --> Proxy : response
Proxy --> PyProxy : Value -> Python object
PyProxy --> User : 0.01

== Set property ==
User -> PyProxy : camera.exposure_time = 0.02
PyProxy -> PyProxy : __setattr__ finds name\nin property_names
PyProxy -> Proxy : SetProperty("exposure_time", value)
Proxy -> Client : MakeRequest("set_property", request)
Client -> Server : ZMQ request
Server -> Svc : dispatch
Svc -> PySvc : invoke PropertySetter(value)
PySvc --> Svc : (new value)
Svc --> Server : reply
Server --> Client : ZMQ reply
Client --> Proxy : response
Proxy --> PyProxy : done

== Execute command ==
User -> PyProxy : dm.apply_shape(channel, shape)\nor proxy.some_command(a=1)
PyProxy -> PyProxy : __getattr__ finds name\nin command_names
PyProxy -> Proxy : ExecuteCommand("some_command", {a: 1})
Proxy -> Client : MakeRequest("execute_command", request)
Client -> Server : ZMQ request
Server -> Svc : dispatch
Svc -> Svc : lookup m_Commands["some_command"]
Svc -> PySvc : Command::Execute(arguments)
PySvc --> Svc : result Value
Svc --> Server : serialized result
Server --> Client : ZMQ reply
Client --> Proxy : response
Proxy --> PyProxy : result -> Python object
PyProxy --> User : result

note over Svc, PySvc
  Properties and commands are registered in Open()
  with make_property() / make_command().
  Handlers must stay responsive; long-running work
  belongs in Main() or a worker thread.
end note

@enduml
